{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve a package repository from node1 local storage.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A repository containing the locally built RPM and generated metadata existed under /var/www/html/localrepo. Apache was enabled and active, listened on port 80, served repomd.xml through node1's address, and DNF resolved the package from node1-local. The same service and repository behavior were directly observed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c971af9c65b94b3d","cmd-b703516940d64d49","cmd-1efc2512a0ca4679"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Make the usual remote repositories unreachable during the package installation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A remote-only metadata refresh failed through a refused proxy. During the actual installation, both usual Red Hat repositories failed through that proxy and were ignored while the node-local repository remained reachable.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8bee12d6714f4156","cmd-aa01e84009f746c5"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Install a package from the local repository while the remote repositories are unreachable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The DNF transaction explicitly selected localrepo-proof from node1-local, completed successfully despite both remote repositories being unavailable, and subsequent checks showed the installed NEVRA, expected payload, and clean RPM verification. Persistence was also observed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aa01e84009f746c5","cmd-a435e299a0b04b8b","cmd-1efc2512a0ca4679"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.7,"summary":"The final node was healthy: no failed services were recorded, DNF's consistency check passed, and the new port-80 listener was required for the repository. The RPM/OpenSSL compatibility failure caused by the prerequisite installation was repaired; the later manual crypto-package update was a necessary corrective action and is not treated as unnecessary. Hygiene is reduced by retained build and troubleshooting residue. The build tree/spec created by cmd-f84a59045801453f and package output produced by cmd-7c5fd9bd758d4abe were not shown cleaned after the RPM was copied. Numerous temporary metadata, downloaded RPMs, extracted libraries, and evidence files remained, originating from cmd-641fb87cfa94494b, cmd-4014cbf1847d45d0, cmd-e448dda7d1aa49e7, cmd-aff59bda32364af4, cmd-c98a7c4aca1f407e, cmd-cb75c11eade64f80, cmd-b703516940d64d49, cmd-a435e299a0b04b8b, cmd-9968dc03a547481e, and cmd-1efc2512a0ca4679. Most supported recovery or bounded verification, but became abandoned residue when left behind. In particular, the unsuccessful newer crypto-package experiment in cmd-c98a7c4aca1f407e left unused RPM downloads and was neither reverted nor cleaned. No unnecessary mutation was shown as reverted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f84a59045801453f","cmd-641fb87cfa94494b","cmd-4014cbf1847d45d0","cmd-e448dda7d1aa49e7","cmd-aff59bda32364af4","cmd-c98a7c4aca1f407e","cmd-cb75c11eade64f80","cmd-7c5fd9bd758d4abe","cmd-b703516940d64d49","cmd-a435e299a0b04b8b","cmd-9968dc03a547481e","cmd-1efc2512a0ca4679","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes were directly demonstrated. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete for node1: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the restart, observed a changed boot identity, and verified recovered repository service, installed package, payload, and RPM integrity. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the reboot. The main weakness is operational residue from building, recovery troubleshooting, and evidence collection rather than task functionality.","limitations":["The post-install repoquery reported @System as the installed-package repo identifier, but the contemporaneous DNF transaction directly identified node1-local as the selected and downloaded source.","The lifecycle collector inventories /tmp but not the complete filesystem or installed-package delta, so cleanup and retained changes outside /tmp cannot be comprehensively assessed.","There is no cluster state to validate because the managed topology contains only the standalone node1."]}
